{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/778122-demonic-pacts-and-abilities","id":778122,"title":"Demonic Pacts and Abilities?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-12-01T22:22:49-08:00","id":778122,"title":"Demonic Pacts and Abilities?","content":"I kind of like the idea of a group of Fallen banding together and using Thralls to train them in specific abilities. But it says that when you increase a Thrall's Ability rating they dint actually gain new knowledge but just an intuitive understanding of a subject. How then can your Thrall train you in Occult, Science, Technology, Medicine, Academics and so on?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-02T01:14:57-08:00","id":778181,"title":"","content":"Hmm, I always played it as such, that the rating given to a Thrall could never go beyond your own capabilitys (though you determine your capabilitys while in your apocalyptic form).<br /> Its a houserule, I know, but it always seemed strange to me, that you could give someone power you didn`t have yourself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6112-seki","name":"Seki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"51"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-02T06:15:16-08:00","id":778282,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mercurial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/778122-demonic-pacts-and-abilities#post778122\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How then can your Thrall train you in Occult, Science, Technology, Medicine, Academics and so on?</div> </div> </div> </div>Simple answer? they can't. If needed they could or call you back to the world, but they wouldn't be able to teach anybody else how to do it.<br /> <br /> This would require you to keep track of which dots were natural (e. they could train you in) and which are from the pact. So if a medical student with Medicine 2 made a pact and ended up with medicine 5 he could teach you the first 2 dots of medicine, but could operate on somebody as if he was a master. I plan to make this the rule in any games I run, as well as the ability to spend a faith point to gain a rating of 5 in an ability for one turn/action (because I'm, also stating angels have a 5 in every ability).<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-02T23:20:36-08:00","id":778827,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/778122-demonic-pacts-and-abilities?p=778181#post778181\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm, I always played it as such, that the rating given to a Thrall could never go beyond your own capabilitys (though you determine your capabilitys while in your apocalyptic form).<br /> Its a houserule, I know, but it always seemed strange to me, that you could give someone power you didn`t have yourself.</div> </div> </div> </div>That isn't how the game describes it, and while it wouldn't make the ability Pacts worthless, most demons wouldn't be able to make one person a talented rockstar and another a brilliant lawyer and another the new Stephen Hawking on campus. Those are part of the Faustian experience that mustn't be lost.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TwoDSix</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/778122-demonic-pacts-and-abilities?p=778282#post778282\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Simple answer? they can't. If needed they could or call you back to the world, but they wouldn't be able to teach anybody else how to do it.<br /> <br /> This would require you to keep track of which dots were natural (e. they could train you in) and which are from the pact. So if a medical student with Medicine 2 made a pact and ended up with medicine 5 he could teach you the first 2 dots of medicine, but could operate on somebody as if he was a master. I plan to make this the rule in any games I run, as well as the ability to spend a faith point to gain a rating of 5 in an ability for one turn/action (because I'm, also stating angels have a 5 in every ability).</div> </div> </div> </div>I could get behind this rule with the stipulation that a Thrall can easily pick up the dates and names of the people and forumulas and theories that are related to his bought Ability through only casual exposure. A Thrall KNOWS about the quadratic formula, but doesn't know the name and might use a different alphabet or symbols to use it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}